        "Making of the Constitution: The Constituent Assembly, formed under the Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946, first met on 9 December 1946 under temporary chairman Dr Sachchidananda Sinha; Dr Rajendra Prasad became its permanent President. Nehru moved the Objectives Resolution on 13 December 1946, the basis of the Preamble. The Drafting Committee (29 August 1947) was chaired by Dr B.R. Ambedkar, with B.N. Rau as Constitutional Adviser. The Constitution was adopted on 26 November 1949 and commenced on 26 January 1950, the date of Purna Swaraj Day 1930. It took 2 years, 11 months and 17 days (many textbooks say 18, counting both end days). The original text had 395 Articles, 22 Parts and 8 Schedules; today there are 25 Parts and 12 Schedules.",
