        "Mnemonic for 1857 leaders: 'Meerut starts, Kanpur Nana, Lucknow Begum, Jhansi Rani, Bareilly Khan' (Khan Bahadur Khan).",
        "Name changes: 1902 United Provinces of Agra and Oudh, 1937 United Provinces, 24 January 1950 Uttar Pradesh, 9 November 2000 Uttarakhand carved out.",
        "Confluence list: Chambal-Yamuna at Etawah; Betwa-Yamuna at Hamirpur; Ken-Yamuna in Banda; Yamuna-Ganga at Prayagraj; Ghaghara-Ganga at Chhapra (Bihar).",
        "Sonbhadra is the only UP district touching four states (MP, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, Bihar) and is the state's power hub: Rihand, Obra, Anpara, Singrauli.",
        "Industry cities: Kanpur leather, Moradabad brass (Peetal Nagri), Firozabad glass (Suhag Nagri), Aligarh locks, Meerut sports goods, Bhadohi carpets, Kannauj ittar.",
        "Numbers to remember: Vidhan Sabha 403, Vidhan Parishad 100, Lok Sabha 80, Rajya Sabha 31; Allahabad High Court 1866, Lucknow bench 1948.",
        "State symbols: animal barasingha (swamp deer), bird sarus crane, flower palash, tree ashoka (NCERT's module lists sal). Dudhwa is the home of the barasingha.",
        "Dialect map from west to east: Khari Boli (Meerut), Braj (Mathura-Agra), Kannauji, Bundeli (Jhansi), Awadhi (Lucknow-Ayodhya), Bhojpuri (Varanasi-Gorakhpur).",
        "UNESCO in UP: four World Heritage Sites as of July 2026: Taj Mahal, Agra Fort and Fatehpur Sikri in Agra district, and the Ancient Buddhist Site of Sarnath (2026) in Varanasi; Ramlila (2008) and Kumbh Mela (2017) as intangible heritage.",
        "Lucknow institutes: CDRI (drugs), NBRI (botany), IITR (toxicology), CIMAP (aromatic plants), Birbal Sahni Institute (palaeobotany), Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research."
