          "answer": "(D) Dyslexia, dysgraphia, dyscalculia, dyspraxia and developmental aphasia. The RPwD Act 2016 lists specific learning disabilities as one of its 21 categories, naming perceptual disabilities, dyslexia, dysgraphia, dyscalculia, dyspraxia and developmental aphasia. The other options are separate categories in the Act."
